  "_reach": "must equal the pulleys' pitch radius: the belt's runs are one radius either side of the axis, and a clamp that is not on a run grips air. 20 teeth at GT2 2 mm is a 12.73 pitch diameter, so 6.365.",
  "_groove": "how far the grip line stands off the carriage. The belt plane is the PITCH circle's plane, which sits 5.5 mm into the pulley from its bore face - so this is not just the clamp's own thickness. fabrica fails the build when it is wrong, which is how 9.5 was arrived at rather than 4."
